75 #edb/ref 17592186344387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344690 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344690 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344690 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344690 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186344022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344690 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6d12dcd5-966c-540d-9792-0af9d3cf5c37" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345207 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345207 #edb/ref 1069 "q-76327" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345207 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345207 #edb/ref 1071 "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are given below. Determine whether $B=\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${a}_{3}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345207 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40af98fe-8e4f-539d-b55b-52163dd7e4ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345207 #edb/ref 1074 "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the RREF matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=-4,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+(-4)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-2)\\cdot (-4)=8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427540 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186427562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427540 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186427563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427540 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186427564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427540 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427540 #edb/ref 1045 "Finding a Basis of a Span" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427540 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186427562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427540 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427540 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049222 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427540 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "81a180d3-6c3b-57f0-9044-6bd27b374a8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427541 #edb/ref 1080 "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427541 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427541 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "04b48259-01c4-5109-abc6-4dc67b3a3146" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427542 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427542 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427542